# Arrowing up through consecutive blank lines must say "blank" every time.
#
# Regression from commit c8a54e1. The arbiter had grown a rule that dropped an
# announcement whose text matched the previous one, added to quieten a list
# boundary. It swallowed every blank line after the first, and the user got
# silence exactly where they needed feedback. Suppressing on CONTENT cannot
# tell "nothing moved" from "the next thing reads the same".

caret "last line"
drain
caret "blank"
drain
caret "blank"
drain
caret "first line"

expect
  last line
  blank
  blank
  first line
